# Argus .trufflehogignore — false-positive path-exclusion list for trufflehog.
#
# trufflehog (as of v3.95.2) has no native per-fingerprint allowlist like
# gitleaks; the closest equivalent is `--exclude-paths` taking a file of
# path/glob entries. This file IS that exclude-paths file.
#
# Canonical scan command (run from repo root):
#   trufflehog git file://. --exclude-paths=.trufflehogignore --no-update --json
#
# Each path below was triaged at MAC-50 [comment 2714377b sibling] and
# board-ratified at MAC-59 [comment b4d9afa0] as a domain false-positive,
# NOT a leaked credential. Future contributors: when adding entries here,
# include a comment block explaining WHY the path is excluded — reviewers
# need to distinguish FPs from accidentally-committed secrets that someone
# tried to hide via allowlist.
#
# Argus-wide invariant: this file MUST stay narrow (per-file path entries).
# Never exclude an entire directory; that would silently skip future
# accidentally-committed secrets in that directory.

